    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-069 -- Viewport-clipped paint architecture.** Fixes the root cause behind ADR-068's GSK GPU crash. HoneyBee no longer hands GSK a ~30,000px DrawingArea surface; the DrawingArea is always viewport-sized.\n\n**Production-verified:** Wikipedia renders correctly with culling ON. `GSK_RENDERER=gl` also works (architectural payoff -- ADR-068's Cairo workaround eliminated the crash, ADR-069 eliminates its cause).\n\n## The architecture\n\n```\nVBox m_content_box\n  top_spacer     (height = scroll_y)\n  DrawingArea    (height = viewport_h)\n  bottom_spacer  (height = content_h - scroll_y - viewport_h)\n```\n\nOn scroll adjustment change: spacers resize, DrawingArea repaints with `cr->translate(0, -scroll_y)` + visible range passed to `pipeline.paint`. Mouse coords in `on_mouse_motion` / `on_link_clicked` get `y += scroll_y`.\n\n## The culling lesson (the actual learning)\n\n**First attempt:** cull in `paint_children` -- skip any child whose layout box is entirely off-screen.\n\n**Bug:** A Box's `y / height` does NOT bound its descendants (absolute positioning, floated figures, overflow:visible). Skipping an off-screen Box skips everything inside it -- including descendants that ARE visible. Wikipedia exposes this: the infobox's tall Box disappears mid-scroll, taking its visible children with it.\n\n**Fix:** cull only leaf nodes (Text / InlineContext). Always recurse into Box nodes; gate only their own paint ops (background, border, shadow, mask, images) on `box_on_screen`.\n\n| Kind | Where culled | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Box | Inside `paint_box`, on paint ops only | Leaf descendants may still be visible |\n| Text | Inside `paint_children`, on the child | No descendants |\n| InlineContext | Inside `paint_children`, on the child | No descendants |\n\n`CULL_MARGIN = 128.0f` covers translateY transform (ADR-058), box-shadow spread, rotate bounding box (ADR-054).\n\n## The diagnostic chain that found the bug\n\n1. Iteration 1: full ADR-069 patch applied; build clean, tests pass, but Wikipedia goes blank mid-scroll.\n2. Iteration 2: added `DRAW-DIAG` fprintf. Tetris math was **correct** (`top + draw + bot = h_px` at every tick), adjustment pointer stable, scroll signal firing.\n3. Iteration 3: `HONEYBEE_NO_CULL=1` test. Content appears. Culling confirmed as the culprit. Root cause: Box y-bound doesn't bound descendants.\n\n**Lesson recorded in ADR:** when culling a tree walk, distinguish leaf nodes (safe to cull) from container nodes (must recurse). \"Box\" does not mean \"opaque rectangle\" -- it means \"a group that might overflow.\"\n\n## Verified (Wikipedia smoke test 2026-11-04)\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| DrawingArea height on Wikipedia | 921px (viewport), not ~30,378px |\n| Content visible at all scroll positions | Yes -- no blank bands |\n| Tim Berners-Lee photo in History | Renders |\n| PNG / SVG / JPEG | All render |\n| Hover on link | Works (`+scroll_y` offset) |\n| Click on link | Works (`+scroll_y` offset) |\n| Scroll smooth | Yes |\n| **`GSK_RENDERER=gl`** | **No crash** -- architectural payoff confirmed |\n| Tests | 691 / 2641 unchanged |\n\n## What this does NOT do\n\n- **Does not remove ADR-068's Cairo setenv.** `setenv(\"GSK_RENDERER\", \"cairo\", 0)` still runs. Belt-and-braces. Removing it is an ADR-070 candidate.\n- **Does not remove Cairo clipping.** Redundant with correct culling; kept as defense-in-depth.\n- **Does not change hover/click logic** except for the `+scroll_y` offset.\n\n## Deferred\n\n- **ADR-070 candidate: remove Cairo fallback.** Now that GSK works, drop the setenv. Needs broader testing across multiple pages.\n- **`Gtk-WARNING: Trying to snapshot gtkmm__GtkBox ... without a current allocation`** -- pre-existing (visible during ADR-069 diagnostics too). Cosmetic.\n- **Full `Gtk::Scrollable` implementation** -- the spacer-tetris pattern works; a proper Scrollable would be cleaner. Deferred.\n- **Sparse content culling** -- per-box cull is already fast on Wikipedia's tree. Not urgent.\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Production-visual, end-to-end with `GSK_RENDERER=gl` proof.**\n\nRefs #274\n",
